STUDY_METHOD=[
"Allocate learning/review time roughly in blueprint order: 44%, 31%, 16%, 9%, then adjust upward for personal weak areas.",
"Learn each concept as a contrast set (e.g., GO vs revenue; market vs limit vs stop; broker vs dealer), not an isolated definition.",
"Immediately follow a lesson with unseen questions on that concept. Do not count paraphrases of an already-seen fact pattern as new questions.",
"Review every miss and every guess: explain why the correct choice wins AND why each plausible distractor fails.",
"Use full-length 75-question mocks in the official 12/33/23/7 scored weighting after coverage is complete.",
"Use the official FINRA practice exam as a calibration of question style, not as a bank to memorize or copy.",
]
